{"parentUuid":"bb7e0f8f-2fa0-403f-9bbb-6289a6ce0500","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01VCM9CZ1b6eB2yC8csRaFDJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Created `/workspace/middleware.ts`.\n\nWhat it does:\n- **`X-Request-Id` header** — sets a fresh UUID on every response via `crypto.randomUUID()` (a Web Crypto global available in Next.js's Edge runtime, no import needed).\n- **Logs the pathname** — `request.nextUrl.pathname` to the console on each request.\n- **`config.matcher`** — runs on all routes except Next.js internals (`_next/static`, `_next/image`) and `favicon.ico`, so you don't spam logs/headers for static assets. Drop the matcher if you'd rather it run on literally every request.\n\nA note on visibility: the header is added to the `NextResponse.next()` response, so it's present on the responses Next emits as the request flows through. The `console.log` appears in your server terminal (or the Edge runtime logs in production) — not the browser console.\n\nYou can confirm it with `npm run dev` and then `curl -i http://localhost:3000/` to see the `X-Request-Id` header in the response."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_read_input_tokens":14026,"output_tokens":419,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":341},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":419,"cache_read_input_tokens":14026,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":341,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbVUKCmRBokyQ5BFAwRUp","type":"assistant","uuid":"e06b8505-33d5-4c80-b51b-a8f52f35cab4","timestamp":"2026-05-28T18:52:31.200Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"